          "type": "turn",
          "question": "I have stage 3 kidney disease and high blood pressure. Does the classification link the two, and what target does guidance describe for someone like me?",
          "answer": "Not medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.\n\n**Does the classification link the two?** Yes, in the coding system. The ICD-10-CM coding guidance says that hypertension with chronic kidney disease moves to code I12, with a second code for the kidney disease stage (coding-hypertension-i10). It also says that where the index links two conditions with \"with,\" the system presumes a relationship unless the record says they are unrelated (coding-type-2-diabetes-e11). This is a rule for how medical records are labeled. It does not tell us what caused your condition, and I can't say whether the two are linked in your case. Your clinician can.\n\n**What target does guidance describe?** The retrieved passages do not give you a number. The hypertension guidance on diagnosis and blood-pressure targets says it covers \"the treatment target most bodies set once treatment has begun,\" but the part with the actual target was not included in what I could retrieve (guideline-hypertension-diagnosis-and-bp-targets). I won't fill that gap from memory. Please ask your clinician or kidney specialist what target applies to you.\n\n**Related points from the guidance:**\n- Adult office readings are classified as normal, elevated, stage 1, or stage 2 hypertension. When the top and bottom numbers fall into different categories, the higher one applies (guideline-hypertension-diagnosis-and-bp-targets).\n- For people with chronic kidney disease, the first-line guidance says renin-angiotensin blockade is preferred. It also says doses are outside its scope (guideline-hypertension-first-line-treatment). Which medicine, if any, suits you is a question for your clinician.\n\nQuestions to bring to your clinician: What blood pressure target applies to me? Is my kidney disease linked to my blood pressure? Which treatment options suit my kidney stage?",
